The triggering relationship is used to model the temporal or causal precedence of behavior elements i"
	      "n a process. The interpretation of a triggering relationship is that some part of the source element "
	      "should be completed before the target element can start. Note that this does not necessarily represen"
	      "t that one behavior element actively starts another; a traffic light turning green also triggers the "
	      "cars to go through the intersection."


